    {
      "id": "c05a0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000017",
      "name": "0. The Parcel Desk",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -64,
        -480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 960,
        "height": 1504,
        "content": "## Challenge 05 \u00b7 The Parcel Desk\n\n**Community Weekly Challenge \u00b7 Season 2**\n\nA shop has **30 parcel requests**. Find the requests that need a correction, then the ones ready for express or standard delivery.\n\n**Starter, not a finished solution.** Build the missing native routing and counting nodes in the three work areas on the right. All three questions use your one personal batch.\n\n### Your dataset\n\n`request_id` \u00b7 `contact_email` \u00b7 `parcel_count` \u00b7 `delivery`\n\nCount **requests, not parcels**. Data and checks follow Challenge 05's participation window.\n\n### Challenge links\n\n[Read Challenge 05](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/challenge-05) \u00b7 [Register](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/register) \u00b7 [Your account](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/status)\n\n[Submit](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/submit) \u00b7 [Results](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/results) \u00b7 [FAQ](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/faq)\n\n[Learn and practise](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/learn) \u00b7 [n8n documentation](https://docs.n8n.io/)"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c05a0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000018",
      "name": "1. Start here",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -32,
        16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 896,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "## 1 \u00b7 Fetch your personal data\n\n[Read Challenge 05](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/challenge-05) and [register](https://marketing.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/cwc/register), or reuse your existing participant key. Enter your forum username and participant key in **Settings**. Keep the supplied base URL and HTTP Authentication **None**. Your key is sent in the `x-participant-key` header, never in the URL.\n\nRun **Start** when Challenge 05 is open. The first successful personal data fetch starts the timer; re-fetching does not reset it. **Request rows** gives 30 items. Fetch your personal requests first."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c05a0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000019",
      "name": "4. Finish and fair play",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -32,
        448
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 896,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "## 4 \u00b7 Finish & fair play\n\n1. **Map your calculated counts** to `b1`, `b2` and `b3` as **Number**. Use a direct native Summarize count of `request_id`; no arithmetic, typed counts, grouped summaries or loops.\n2. **Check when ready.** Checks start disabled, are optional and never stop the timer.\n3. **Submit all three counts, your workflow JSON and your explanation.** Correct eligible answers enter the leaderboard immediately; the first accepted evidence stays locked.\n\n**Timing:** first successful personal fetch \u2192 first accepted final. Weekly points are **15 / 12 / 12 / 11** by competition rank.\n\n**No AI assistance of any kind**, including interpreting, planning, generating, debugging, solving or explaining this challenge. Chatbots, copilots, workflow builders and agents are included. No Code, Function, AI, Agent, MCP or Tool nodes.\n\n**Before export:** blank Settings.key, set Authentication to None and remove all credential references and pinned data.\n\nWorkflows are reviewed at season end before rewards."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c05a0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000020",
      "name": "Stage 1: Needs correction",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        928,
        -480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 1152,
        "height": 480,
        "content": "## Question 1 \u00b7 Needs correction\n\nCount requests with an empty contact email OR zero parcels. If both are wrong, count that request once. Delivery does not rescue an invalid request.\n\n**Your work area:** add native validation/routing and **Summarize \u2192 Count `request_id`**.\n\nMap the calculated field directly to **Stage 1 answer \u2192 b1** as **Number**. Keep enabled forward paths from Request rows through your calculation to this answer. The Check node is optional.\n\n**Build your calculation in the space below.**"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c05a0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000021",
      "name": "Stage 2: Express ready",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        928,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 1152,
        "height": 480,
        "content": "## Question 2 \u00b7 Express ready\n\nCount valid requests whose delivery is EXPRESS. Validate before choosing the delivery queue.\n\n**Your work area:** add native validation/routing and **Summarize \u2192 Count `request_id`**.\n\nMap the calculated field directly to **Stage 2 answer \u2192 b2** as **Number**. Keep enabled forward paths from Request rows through your calculation to this answer. The Check node is optional.\n\n**Build your calculation in the space below.**"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c05a0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000022",
      "name": "Stage 3: Standard ready",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        928,
        544
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 1152,
        "height": 480,
        "content": "## Question 3 \u00b7 Standard ready\n\nCount valid requests whose delivery is STANDARD. The three calculated queue counts should add up to 30.\n\n**Your work area:** add native validation/routing and **Summarize \u2192 Count `request_id`**.\n\nMap the calculated field directly to **Stage 3 answer \u2192 b3** as **Number**. Keep enabled forward paths from Request rows through your calculation to this answer. The Check node is optional.\n\n**Build your calculation in the space below.**"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
